<body><main><header><a href={base}>Valen</a><nav><a href={`${base}archive/`}>Archive</a><a class="active" href={`${base}about/`}>About</a></nav></header>
<article><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Software, systems, and the space between them.</h1><p>I’m Valentín Liñeiro, a software engineer interested in architecture, developer productivity, and the changing relationship between people and software.</p><p>I spend most of my time trying to make complex systems easier to understand and easier to change. That usually means looking for friction before reaching for more machinery.</p><p>More recently, I’ve been exploring how AI changes the economics of software development: when execution becomes cheaper, the valuable part of engineering shifts toward framing problems, making decisions, and learning from the result.</p><p>This site is where I keep the ideas that survive that process.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/valentinlineiro">GitHub</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/valentinlineiro/">LinkedIn</a><a href={`${base}rss.xml`}>RSS</a></div></article>
<footer><a href={base}>← Home</a></footer></main></body></html>
